## Phase F: the mouse language (user: "lets start now", "avoid all keyboard interactions")

Decisions (user, 2026-09-27): the zones as proposed; keys only Space, Esc, Enter, D (programmable) plus the arrow keys for next / previous image and folder; save folder = the user's Documents folder; clipboard paste; start-up time into a log.

**Profile** (new `source\mouse\uMouseProfile.pas`, file `Default.mouse` next to MView.ini, written with the built-in profile at the first start):
- Four zones (the quarters), each with a name shown on screen, an optional browsing order (Date / Name) and its own event table; `[Anywhere]` for what a zone doesn't set; `[Keys]` for Space / Esc / Enter / D.
- Events: left / right click and double-click, wheel up / down / click, tilt left / right, X1, X2, gestures left / right / up / down. Up to three commands per event ("WheelDown = SortByName, NextImage"); "None" switches an Anywhere entry off in a zone. Command names instead of Hamana's numbers; unknown lines are reported (line number) and skipped.
- Default: top left "Edit" (wheel turns 5 degrees, double-click = edit mode), top right "Browse by name", bottom left "Browse by date", bottom right "Inspect" (wheel zooms at the mouse). Anywhere: wheel = next / previous image, double-click = fit <-> 100 %, right click = menu, wheel click = fullscreen, tilt and gestures left / right = previous / next folder, gesture up = parent folder, gesture down = exit, X1 / X2 = zoom / rotate mode (as before).

**Engine** (new `source\mouse\uMouseEngine.pas`, replaces the fixed controls of uInputHandler, which is no longer used):
- Zones with a dead band of 3 % along the middle lines (the zone doesn't flicker there); fixed while a button is held.
- A zone's name appears in its corner for 1.5 s when the mouse enters it and with each command from it; a gesture shows what it will do in the middle of the window while it is made (back to the start = nothing).
- A single click runs at once, unless that zone also has a double-click for the button: then it waits for the Windows double-click time.
- Tilt: one event per tilt (holding repeats are ignored for 300 ms). X1 / X2 on the press (as before), Browser Back / Forward keys count as X1 / X2 except as an echo.
- Navigation from a zone with an order switches to that order first (only if different; the current image stays).
- Fixed: left drag = pan, right drag = gesture, arrow keys, Ctrl+V = paste. The other old keys (+, -, Home, End, L, R, S, F5, I, Z) are gone.
- Menu: now a command (right click by default), no longer the LCL's automatic one; entries: Paste image, Save image, Save image and view (debugging), Exit.
- The cursor hides after [Mouse] MouseCursorHideTime without input.

**Settings editor, "Mouse & keys" page** (new `source\config\uMousePage.pas`): the zones as a picture (click a zone, Anywhere or Keys), name and order of a zone, per event up to three commands from lists ("(as in Anywhere: ...)" / "(nothing here)" for zones); "Try it here": a small area with the same zones and a real engine with the profile being edited: every button, wheel, tilt, side button and key shows what arrived and what it would run. Save / Undo / Exit / View images cover both pages.

**Paste and save:** "Paste image" (menu, Ctrl+V) shows the clipboard's image ("Clipboard image ... not saved"), until the next step. "Save image" writes only the image (PNG) to [Debug] SaveImageDirectory; if that is empty, the user's Documents folder (SHGetFolderPath, also when moved to OneDrive), which is then written into MView.ini. The old save (image and a picture of the window) stays as "Save image and view (debugging)".

**Start-up:** `startup.csv` next to MView.exe (with TimingLog=1): exe size, ms from process start to the window, OpenGL set-up, view ready, first image painted.

**Diagnostics line** in two lines (it ran past the right edge on a full-HD screen).

Tests: new `test\TestMouse.lpr` (plain fpc, in build_test.bat): profile parsing, errors with line numbers, save / load round trip, zones and dead band, the engine with a fake clock (zone order, wheel parts, zoom / turn smoothness, click vs double-click timing, drag, menu, gestures and preview, tilt repeat, X1 mode and Browser Back echo, Esc, keys, focus lost).

Not compiled here (no Free Pascal in the sandbox); reviewed independently before committing.

Review (two independent reviews, engine / integration) found and fixed: a test constant named TRY (a reserved word); PtInRect needing the Types unit; a double-click could span two zones; a right click moved about 22 px diagonally gave neither menu nor gesture (the two thresholds now agree); tilting the other way within 300 ms was ignored; ";" or "#" inside a zone name was cut as a comment; a UTF-8 byte order mark broke the first line; a click waiting for its double-click could run with a newly set profile; the cursor could hide while the menu was open; a paste made with no file open had no info line; a second paste could show the first one's "saved as"; Save / Undo on the mouse page focused the hidden text editor; no false "changed" from programmatic updates of the order and name. Predicted: every TestMouse check passes.

Note: this MView.ini has SaveImageDirectory=...\test\saved_images\ (the old default, written by earlier versions), so saves still go there; delete the value to use the Documents folder.

After the first test (user): the zone names now only appear while the diagnostics line is on (D); otherwise distracting ("they show all right and long enough to see"). "Mouse & keys" page: the three boxes of a row got headings (Command / then / and then) and the explanation says that one press runs a row's commands from left to right; the zone cells show caption, name and order on separate lines, cut at the cell's edges instead of running over.

Arrow keys changed (user): up / down = previous / next image, left / right = previous / next folder (like the wheel and the gestures / tilt). TestMouse checks each arrow on its own.

## Edit mode: select and crop (user)

"single left click in the edit field enables edit mode, double left click disables it; edit mode enables a selection box and in the right-click menu 'crop selection'; the cropped selection is zoomed to screen and can be saved with Save image."
- Profile: new commands EditModeOn, EditModeOff, CropSelection (EditMode = on / off stays). Built-in Edit zone (top left): LeftClick = EditModeOn, LeftDouble = EditModeOff (the click waits for the double-click time there, as designed). An existing Default.mouse keeps its old entries: the "Mouse & keys" page has a new button "Use the built-in profile" (then Save).
- Edit mode: the mode label says "EDIT ... left drag = select an area, right click: Crop selection, double-click in the Edit zone / Esc = end". Left drag draws the selection instead of panning (the engine now also reports where a drag starts and is: cmdDragStart / cmdDragPoint). The selection is kept in original image pixels, so it stays on the image while zooming (and is drawn turned with the image); both renderers draw it as a dark / light frame. A new image clears it; the full version of the same image keeps it. Switching edit mode on starts the full-size decode.
- Menu: "Crop selection" (only shown in edit mode, enabled with a selection). The area is cut from the best version in memory (the full image; the quick view if the full one isn't there yet, the info line says so; the frame on screen of a playing animation), shown fitted to the screen with the same rotation, as "Cropped from <name>". Save image writes <name>_crop_<time>.png. A crop can be cropped again; the next step goes back to the files.
- Esc (Back): the zoom / rotate mode first, then edit mode, then exit (the engine sends Back to TMView, which knows about edit mode).
Tests: TestMouse: Edit zone click = on (after the double-click time), double-click = off; drag start / point reported; Esc = Back.

## Zones switch, overlay options (user, end of the day)

- **Zones on / off:** [Mouse] ZonesEnabled=1 (default) / 0 in MView.ini. Off: every button does its Anywhere command everywhere; no zone orders, no zone names. The "Mouse & keys" page has a green / red button at the top left ("Zones ON" / "Zones OFF: only Anywhere counts"); it writes the line into the MView.ini text of the editor (saved with Save, like any other change); the zone picture says "(zones off)", and "Try it here" follows the switch. TestMouse: zones off, the bottom right wheel steps images instead of zooming.
- **Overlay readability** ([View] in MView.ini):
  - OverlaySolid=0 (default) / 1: the info and diagnostics lines on a solid black bar across the window instead of straight over the image.
  - OverlayColor=White (default) / Yellow / Red: colour of the texts over the image (info, diagnostics, mode label, zone name, gesture text); both renderers (GPU: the white text texture tinted, so no extra cost).
- A renderer made when switching to fullscreen now also takes over edit mode (it lost the EDIT label before).

## Esc: back to the settings screen (user, after the test)

"if esc is in image view mode, hitting esc does not exit, it opens the main screen with ini editor (as if started without image). in edit mode esc leaves edit mode, in the main editor esc exits the program."
- Esc is now a fixed key (no longer in the profile's [Keys]; an old "Esc = Back" line in Default.mouse is ignored, the "Mouse & keys" page no longer shows an Esc row). In the viewer: zoom / rotate mode off, else edit mode off, else back to the settings screen.
- Back to the settings screen: the viewer ends as on exit (fullscreen off, window place and settings saved, threads stopped), the views and the menu are freed, the settings editor shows with MView.ini and Default.mouse read again. "View images" or a dropped file starts a fresh viewer. The switch runs after the key handler (QueueAsyncCall), because the view that handles the key is freed.
- On the settings screen Esc = Exit (with unsaved changes, the first press warns, a second one leaves). Not while "Try it here" has the focus (it tries Esc out) or a drop-down list is open.
- The Back command from a gesture or button (if the profile maps one) does the same as Esc; Exit stays Exit.
Tests: TestMouse: Esc not in the saved profile, old Esc line ignored, second Esc = Back (not Exit).
Review (independent) found and fixed: a held Esc (key repeat) or a quick second Esc could reach the settings screen and end MView at once (the Esc that left the viewer is now ignored until released); the viewer's shutdown could wait forever for a worker stuck in a read (the exit deadline of the watchdog now covers it and is disarmed afterwards; uWatchdog.DisarmExitDeadline); a second viewer wrote a misleading startup.csv row (skipped); "Try it here" now answers Esc with what Back does.

First test (user): Esc to the settings screen crashed (access violation in uMouseEngine FocusLost): freeing a view moves the focus away inside its inherited destructor, and its DoExit used the mouse engine it had just freed. Fixed in both views (uMediaView, uGLMediaView): DoExit checks the engine is still there.

## Where the day ends

Built today (Day 19, 2026-09-27): failsafe against lockups (emergency exit, exit deadline, memory guard, stuck-disk handling, no disk access on the window thread); own LZW TIFF reader (parallel, 2-3 x faster than Hamana by the user's comparison); GIF animation (own decoder, frame clock, test suite passes); PNG / BMP through WIC in bands (NASA 21600 x 21600 images open, Hamana skips them); Phase F: the mouse language (zones, profile file, settings page with "Try it here"), edit mode with selection and crop, paste from the clipboard, save image, start-up log; spec v1.3.
Tests (user's run 16:11): 87 + 40 + 58 + 198 passed, 0 failed (before the edit mode and zones switch checks were added).

