## A homage to Hamana (user: "i want it to be a hommage to hamana ... all of this is important")

- readme.md: the dedication at the top (Hamana by Makito Miyano, last version 1.48, 2006; "fast first, mouse first, never in the way"), how to use MView, the documentation map, the principles.
- Menu: "About MView" (above Exit) shows what MView is and the dedication (uMainForm, AboutText, Application.MessageBox).
- docs\From_Hamana_to_MView.md / .docx: why the homage, Hamana in brief (from its own readme, v1.45, 2005-10-10: DirectX drawing, read-ahead with no waiting, no registry, written for a GeForce 3), what MView kept, what it changed and why, the Hamana profile, the principle, respect (no Hamana code, formats, artwork or text; the name belongs to its author).
- mouse\Hamana.mouse (and a copy next to MView.ini in build\): Hamana's mouse as set up in the user's Hamana.key: wheel = images by name at the top right, by date at the bottom left, zoom elsewhere; the four gestures; right click = original size; wheel click / Enter = fullscreen; Space = next image. MView's own choices where Hamana had none or differed: X1 = zoom mode, X2 = menu, top-left click / double-click = edit mode on / off, tilt = folders, one thing per zone. Switch in MView.ini: [Mouse] Profile=Hamana.mouse (back: Profile=Default.mouse). The file must exist first, or MView writes its default profile under that name.
- Spec: §1.1 the homage, §2.0 the first principle "Fast first, mouse first, never in the way", §9.2 other profiles.
- The Back command's caption now says "else the settings screen" (it said "else exit" since Esc changed).
- Review (independent) found and fixed: the ini key is Profile, not MouseProfile (the instructions would have done nothing); the menu on a right double-click made every right click wait for the double-click time and opened the menu with the button still held (now on X2, the right click is instant); the X2 wording; the cursor could come back hidden after the About box.
- Tests: TestMouse loads the shipped mouse\Hamana.mouse: no errors, zones and orders, gestures, buttons, keys; the engine with it: top right = by name then next image, bottom right = zoom in, right click = original size at once, X2 = menu.

